Fork edits of upstream files under desktop-apps/package/ (the submodule stays
untouched). build/.docker/packages.bake.Dockerfile applies this after copying
the build/linux/package/ overlay (new files, see its fork.mk):

  patch -p1 --forward --fuzz=0 < package.patch     (in desktop-apps/package)

--fuzz=0 makes upstream drift fail the build instead of patching the wrong
place. To change or rebase it, edit a copy of the files and regenerate with
"diff -ru a b" from a directory holding the original (a/) and edited (b/) tree.

  deb/template/control.m4  Homepage field (PUBLISHER_URL)
  deb/template/postrm.m4   purge removes what postinst wrote: the .sources
                           and defaults files if still ours, the keyring
                           (UnityStack's, shared with its other products'
                           repositories) if no other apt source uses it
  rpm/common.spec          %post registers the repository like the deb
                           postinst (zypp or yum directory by distribution),
                           %postun on erase removes it again; ships
                           the metainfo and the rpm-only payload (repository
                           key); fixes the "euro-office" comparison, which
                           never matched COMPANY_NAME "Euro-Office" (no help
                           subpackage, no /usr/bin/desktopeditors, and a
                           mode-777 /etc/<package> directory)
  rpm/requires.spec        Requires by soname and "Fedora or openSUSE" font
                           names, so the one RPM also installs on openSUSE
                           (Fedora package names such as boost-filesystem or
                           xcb-util-cursor do not exist there), and on EL10
                           without EPEL (no libXss)

