+# One RPM for Fedora/RHEL and openSUSE, whose package names differ (libX11
+# vs libX11-6, xcb-util-cursor vs libxcb-cursor0, ...): libraries by soname,
+# which both generate (only 64-bit packages are built), fonts as "Fedora
+# name or openSUSE name". Narrow is a separate package only on Fedora/EL
+# (openSUSE's liberation-fonts holds it, or has none), so it is required
+# only there; "or liberation-fonts" would let dnf skip it. boost-filesystem
+# is gone: boost is linked statically, no binary needs a system one; so is
+# libXScrnSaver, which no binary links or loads (and EL10 lacks without EPEL).
+# NSS, ALSA, GBM, DRM, GL/EGL, X11-xcb and PulseAudio: linked directly by
